; Map KEYS in the Special CBOR class (bool — major type 7) share their major type with the
; indefinite-length break byte (0xff). A stale IR assert rejected any named table with such a key
; at generation time; the definite-length map loop reads exactly n entries and never inspects for
; a break (`make_deser_loop_break_check` gates on the INDEFINITE case only), and the indefinite map
; loop probes the break with the non-consuming `special_break()` so a bool key is read normally —
; so a bool-keyed table is deserializable in both framings (indefinite covered by the
; golden_hex_preserve bool_table_indef KAT).
bkeys = { * bool => uint }
; referencing the named special-key table as a record field is the shape that hit the assert
; (it fired in `new_type` on the resolved reference); the inline form exercises the same key wire
; path through a field-local map, whose emit-tests mint puts a real bool key on the wire.
bkey_holder = [named: bkeys, inline: { * bool => uint }]

; A named exact table stays a transparent alias to its checked BoundedMap carrier. The holder makes
; emitted tests mint that alias at an embed site, exercising the checked TryFrom construction door.
bkeys_exact = { bool => uint }
bkey_exact_holder = [bounded: bkeys_exact]
